+## Fulfilment webhook
+
+Every insert into `public.orders` POSTs the new row as JSON to the fulfilment partner
+(migration `order_fulfilment_webhook`). The URL and shared secret are not in the repo.
+They live in Supabase Vault. Each project needs them set once, in the SQL editor:
+
+```sql
+select vault.create_secret('<FULFILMENT_WEBHOOK_URL>',    'fulfilment_webhook_url');
+select vault.create_secret('<FULFILMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET>', 'fulfilment_webhook_secret');
+```
+
+Values come from `.env.local`. If either secret is missing, inserts into `orders` fail
+with an error, so orders are never dropped silently.
+
 Test accounts on the hosted project: `alice@example.com`, `bob@example.com` and
 `carol@example.com`, all with the password `trailhead-test-1`.
